---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Notice from '../../components/Notice.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { product } from '../../data/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'before-you-start', label: 'Before you start' },
  { id: 'get-the-file', label: 'Get the tarball' },
  { id: 'verify', label: 'Verify the file' },
  { id: 'install', label: 'Install in a separate folder' },
  { id: 'check', label: 'Check that it works' },
  { id: 'troubleshooting', label: 'If something fails' },
  { id: 'remove', label: 'Removing it' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quick Start"
  accent="Install for the private alpha."
  description="Install the Flowprint 0.1.0-alpha.5 private-alpha tarball: check Node.js, verify the SHA-256, install into a separate folder with npm or pnpm."
  lead="Install the Flowprint tarball you received into its own folder — never inside the repository you want to analyze — and confirm that it runs. Takes a few minutes."
  toc={toc}
>
  <Notice title="Closed test" tone="alpha">
    <p>
      Flowprint is only available to invited testers. There is no public download and no npm package. Please do not
      share the file or forward it.
    </p>
  </Notice>

  <Section id="before-you-start" title="Before you start" n={1}>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <p><strong>Check your Node.js version.</strong></p>
        <CodeBlock code="node --version" label="Any shell" />
        <p>
          It must satisfy <code>{product.nodeEngines}</code>: 20.19.0 or newer within 20.x, or 22.12.0 or newer.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <strong>Make sure you can reach the npm registry.</strong> Installing the tarball still downloads Flowprint's
          dependencies — including a native parser binary for your platform — from the public npm registry. Offline
          installation is not supported. Behind a corporate proxy, npm must already be configured for it.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          <strong>Use npm or pnpm.</strong> Yarn Classic (v1) is not supported for installing this file.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <Notice title="Do not install inside the repository you will analyze" tone="warn">
      <p>
        Use the separate folder described below, so the analyzed repository's <code>package.json</code> and lockfile stay
        untouched. Flowprint does not need to live next to the code it reads.
      </p>
    </Notice>
  </Section>

  <Section id="get-the-file" title="Get the tarball" n={2}>
    <p>
      Your facilitator sends you <code>{product.tarball}</code> directly — by file share, email, or chat. It is not
      downloadable from this site, npm, or GitHub. You do not need to clone the Flowprint repository.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section id="verify" title="Verify the file" n={3}>
    <p>
      In the folder that contains the downloaded file, run the command for your system and compare the result with the
      expected SHA-256 below.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock code={`sha256sum ${product.tarball}`} label="Linux" />
    <CodeBlock code={`shasum -a 256 ${product.tarball}`} label="macOS" />
    <CodeBlock code={`Get-FileHash .\\${product.tarball} -Algorithm SHA256`} label="Windows PowerShell" />
    <p>Expected SHA-256 for <code>{product.tarball}</code>:</p>
    <CodeBlock code={product.tarballSha256} label="SHA-256" />
    <p>
      PowerShell prints the same value in uppercase; the comparison is case-insensitive. If the value differs, stop and
      tell your facilitator.
    </p>
    <Notice title="The checksum belongs to one exact build">
      <p>
        This value is only valid for the alpha.5 tarball listed here. If you receive a rebuilt tarball, it comes with a
        new checksum — use that one.
      </p>
    </Notice>
  </Section>

  <Section id="install" title="Install in a separate folder" n={4}>
    <p>
      The commands below work the same in bash, zsh, Windows PowerShell, and cmd. Run them one line at a time. First
      create a folder and move into it:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock code={`mkdir flowprint-test\ncd flowprint-test`} label="Any shell" />
    <p>
      Copy <code>{product.tarball}</code> into this <code>flowprint-test</code> folder, then install with
      <strong>one</strong> of the following.
    </p>
    <h3>npm</h3>
    <CodeBlock code={`npm init -y\nnpm install ./${product.tarball}`} label="npm" />
    <h3>pnpm</h3>
    <CodeBlock code={`pnpm init\npnpm add ./${product.tarball}`} label="pnpm" />
  </Section>

  <Section id="check" title="Check that it works" n={5}>
    <p>Still inside <code>flowprint-test</code>:</p>
    <CodeBlock code="npx flowprint --version" label="Any shell" />
    <p>Expected output:</p>
    <CodeBlock code={`flowprint ${product.version}`} label="Output" copy={false} />
    <p>
      Flowprint is installed locally in this folder, not on your <code>PATH</code>, so always run it as
      <code>npx flowprint</code> from <code>flowprint-test</code>. The full option list is in the
      <a href="/docs/cli-reference">CLI Reference</a>.
    </p>
    <Notice title="Taking part in a facilitated session?">
      <p>
        Please do not run Flowprint on any repository before your session. Your facilitator will tell you which
        repository to use. Otherwise, continue with <a href="/docs/first-analysis">First Analysis</a>.
      </p>
    </Notice>
  </Section>

  <Section id="troubleshooting" title="If something fails" n={6}>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>npx asks to install a package.</strong> Answer <em>no</em>. It means you are not inside
        <code>flowprint-test</code> or the install did not complete — Flowprint is not published to npm, so there is
        nothing to download.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>“parser native binding not found for this platform”.</strong> The native parser dependency did not
        install. Delete <code>node_modules</code> and the lockfile in <code>flowprint-test</code> and install again with
        registry access.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Yarn Classic error</strong> <code>Received malformed response from registry</code>: Yarn v1 is not
        supported. Use npm or pnpm.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Anything else:</strong> copy the full error message and send it to your facilitator. Please do not spend
        more than 10 minutes troubleshooting.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Section>

  <Section id="remove" title="Removing it" n={7}>
    <p>Delete the <code>flowprint-test</code> folder. Nothing else was installed.</p>
  </Section>
</DocsLayout>
